# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Ignore everything, then name the few files that belong in the repository.
#
# A whitelist rather than a blacklist, because the repository holds only what
# cannot be regenerated. Everything else -- the pbf, the road and elevation
# databases, the coverage grids, the maps, the rides -- comes back from the
# commands in commandes_bases.txt, so Git has no business carrying it.
#
# Git does not look inside an ignored folder, so Data/, Maps/ and Runs/ are
# skipped whole: nothing from them can slip in by accident.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #

*

!.gitignore
!tilehunt.py
!COMMANDES_BASE.txt

# The tests cannot be regenerated either. Uncomment these two lines to keep
# them, which is worth doing the day you change the tile maths or the solver.
# !test_*.py
# !*.mjs